%% Current state. Sources: dispute APIs and verification dispute handlers. Verified 2026-09-13.
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> RESULT_IN: ACIC result stored
    RESULT_IN --> DISPUTE_WINDOW_OPEN: DCO / OpenDisputeWindow
    RESULT_IN --> COMPLETED: NDCO or non-DCO finalisation

    DISPUTE_WINDOW_OPEN --> DISPUTE_WINDOW_CLOSED: Applicant accepts result / waive
    DISPUTE_WINDOW_OPEN --> DISPUTE_WINDOW_CLOSED: 48h deadline reached / sweep
    DISPUTE_WINDOW_OPEN --> DISPUTE_RAISED: Applicant raises singleton dispute

    DISPUTE_RAISED --> DISPUTE_RAISED: Admin replies / asks for evidence
    DISPUTE_RAISED --> DISPUTE_RAISED: Customer adds message
    DISPUTE_RAISED --> MANUAL_REVIEW: Admin escalates
    DISPUTE_RAISED --> DISPUTE_WINDOW_CLOSED: Applicant withdraws
    DISPUTE_RAISED --> DISPUTE_WINDOW_CLOSED: Admin resolves ORIGINAL_STANDS
    DISPUTE_RAISED --> DISPUTE_WINDOW_CLOSED: Admin resolves AMENDED

    DISPUTE_WINDOW_CLOSED --> COMPLETED: close-dispute-window finalises
    COMPLETED --> [*]
    MANUAL_REVIEW --> [*]

    note right of DISPUTE_WINDOW_OPEN
      Applicant can view DCO detail. Window is 5m sandbox, 48h prod.
      Certificate and external delivery are held.
    end note

    note right of DISPUTE_RAISED
      Dispute header is SK=DISPUTE.
      Thread messages use DISPUTEMSG#...
      Admin queue uses GSI8 DISPUTE#OPEN.
    end note

    note right of DISPUTE_WINDOW_CLOSED
      Certificate and delivery are best-effort.
      Delivery failures are observable and retryable.
    end note
